----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BADGE CONTROLLER -> CAR, WITHOUT HARDWARE
There is no badge on this machine's USB and the car is at the venue, so nothing here was flashed
or run. What can be checked off-hardware is checked: both firmwares build with the repository's own
toolchain, and the bytes the two sides will exchange are compared field by field.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

====================================================================================================
1. PROTOCOL AGREEMENT — one wire format, two firmwares
====================================================================================================
  [ok ] every protocol constant matches between the badge and the car
        ESPNOW_MAGIC_0 = 'B' (badge) / 'B' (car)
        ESPNOW_MAGIC_1 = 'C' (badge) / 'C' (car)
        ESPNOW_VERSION = 1 (badge) / 1 (car)
        ESPNOW_KIND_DRIVE = 1 (badge) / 1 (car)
        ESPNOW_KIND_STATUS = 2 (badge) / 2 (car)
        ESPNOW_CHANNEL = 1 (badge) / 1 (car)
        ESPNOW_PAIR_KEY = 0x5A17BAD6u (badge) / 0x5A17BAD6u (car)
        ESPNOW_FLAG_STOP = 0x01 (badge) / 0x01 (car)
        ESPNOW_STATUS_ESPNOW_DRIVING = 0x01 (badge) / 0x01 (car)
        ESPNOW_STATUS_DEADMAN = 0x02 (badge) / 0x02 (car)
        ESPNOW_STATUS_INTERVAL_MS = 500 (badge) / 500 (car)
        ESPNOW_DRIVE_BYTES = 16 (badge) / 16 (car)
        ESPNOW_STATUS_BYTES = 18 (badge) / 18 (car)
  [ok ] both structs are the same fields, in the same order, with the same types
        differs: []

  BadgeCarStatus — 18 bytes on the air:
      +  0  uint8_t        magic[2]
      +  2  uint8_t        version
      +  3  uint8_t        kind
      +  4  uint32_t       pairKey
      +  8  uint16_t       seq
      + 10  uint16_t       uptime100ms
      + 12  int16_t        left
      + 14  int16_t        right
      + 16  uint8_t        flags
      + 17  uint8_t        reserved

  BadgeDrivePacket — 16 bytes on the air:
      +  0  uint8_t        magic[2]
      +  2  uint8_t        version
      +  3  uint8_t        kind
      +  4  uint32_t       pairKey
      +  8  int16_t        left
      + 10  int16_t        right
      + 12  uint16_t       seq
      + 14  uint8_t        flags
      + 15  uint8_t        reserved

